# Domain Layer

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/backend.md`, `docs/architecture/persistence.md`.

## Rules

- Pure TypeScript only
- Repository **ports** live in `packages/domain/<context>/ports`
- May depend on `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/shared-kernel-types` and Zod
- Never import NestJS, TypeORM, Redis, `contracts`, `application`, or `infrastructure`

## Allowed

```typescript
import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto'
import { z } from 'zod'
import type { TenantId, UserId } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/shared-kernel-types'
```

## Forbidden

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common'
import { Entity, Column } from 'typeorm'
import { InviteMemberInput } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts'
```

## Aggregate Example

```typescript
// packages/domain/src/tenancy/tenant.ts
import type { TenantId } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/shared-kernel-types'
import type { DomainEvent } from '../shared-kernel/domain-event'

export class Tenant {
  private constructor(
    readonly id: TenantId,
    private name: string,
    private status: 'active' | 'suspended',
  ) {}

  static create(id: TenantId, name: string): { tenant: Tenant; events: DomainEvent[] } {
    const tenant = new Tenant(id, name, 'active')
    return {
      tenant,
      events: [{ type: 'TenantCreated', tenantId: id, occurredAt: new Date() }],
    }
  }

  rename(name: string): DomainEvent[] {
    if (!name.trim()) throw new InvalidTenantNameError()
    this.name = name.trim()
    return [{ type: 'TenantRenamed', tenantId: this.id, name: this.name, occurredAt: new Date() }]
  }

  suspend(): DomainEvent[] {
    if (this.status === 'suspended') throw new TenantAlreadySuspendedError()
    this.status = 'suspended'
    return [{ type: 'TenantSuspended', tenantId: this.id, occurredAt: new Date() }]
  }
}
```

## Repository Port (in domain)

```typescript
// packages/domain/src/tenancy/ports/tenant.repository.ts
import type { TenantId } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/shared-kernel-types'
import type { Tenant } from '../tenant'

export interface TenantRepository {
  findById(id: TenantId): Promise<Tenant | null>
  save(tenant: Tenant): Promise<void>
}
```

## Context Isolation

Do not import another context's internals (`tenancy` must not import `authorization` domain types). Reference by ID only (`UserId`, `TenantId`, `RoleId` from `shared-kernel-types`).

## Testing

Unit-test aggregates with Vitest — no Nest/DB/Redis. Target ~90% coverage on `packages/domain`.
